  "title": "lab5-dev-notes",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "kernel/vm.c",
      "description": "Modify uvmcopy() to map the parent's physical pages into the child, instead of allocating new pages. Clear PTE_W in the PTEs of both child and parent.",
      "line": 314
    },
    {
      "file": "kernel/vm.c",
      "description": "It may be useful to have a way to record, for each PTE, whether it is a COW mapping. You can use the RSW (reserved for software) bits in the RISC-V PTE for this.",
      "line": 315
    },
    {
      "file": "kernel/vm.c",
      "description": "don't free physical memory as the parent is using it",
      "line": 325
    },
    {
      "file": "kernel/trap.c",
      "description": "Ensure that each physical page is freed when the last PTE reference to it goes away -- but not before. A good way to do this is to keep, for each physical page, a \"reference count\" of the number of user page tables that refer to that page. Set a page's reference count to one when kalloc() allocates it. Increment a page's reference count when fork causes a child to share the page, and decrement a page's count each time any process drops the page from its page table. kfree() should only place a page back on the free list if its reference count is zero. It's OK to to keep these counts in a fixed-size array of integers. You'll have to work out a scheme for how to index the array and how to choose its size. For example, you could index the array with the page's physical address divided by 4096, and give the array a number of elements equal to highest physical address of any page placed on the free list by kinit() in kalloc.c.",
      "line": 68
    },
    {
      "file": "kernel/trap.c",
      "description": "原本这里我写的\n// change the page mapping of current process\n        if (mappages(p->pagetable, va, PGSIZE, (uint64)new_pa, flags) != 0) {\n          kfree(new_pa);\n          p->killed = 1;\n        }\n\n但是这个页面地址va已经被映射到原来的old_pa了，这里应该直接修改PTE。",
      "line": 110
    },
    {
      "file": "kernel/vm.c",
      "description": "Modify copyout() to use the same scheme as page faults when it encounters a COW page.\n\n这个要求是让 copyout() 函数在遇到COW页面时使用与页面错误相同的处理方案。copyout() 是内核函数，用于将数据从内核空间复制到用户空间，但COW页面在内核中直接写入时不会触发页面错误，所以需要手动检查和处理。\n\n为什么COW页面在内核中直接写入时不会触发页面错误？\n\n​1. 特权级别差异​\n\nCPU在核心态（内核模式）运行时完全绕过硬件级别的页面权限检查​\nCOW页面标记的\"只读\"属性仅适用于用户态程序\n内核模式有完整的访问权限，包括写入只读页面的能力\n\n​2. 硬件行为特点​\n\n页面错误仅在执行用户代码时发生\n核心态下处理器不会检查PTE的读写权限位\nMMU默认信任内核代码具有正确权限\n\n后果与风险\n\n​违反COW语义​：内核的直接写入会破坏共享物理页，导致多个进程看到彼此的非预期修改\n\n​内存一致性问题​：数据写入不会更新页表权限，用户态下次访问时状态不一致\n\n​安全风险​：允许内核绕过正常的内存保护机制",
      "line": 351
    },
    {
      "file": "kernel/kalloc.c",
      "description": "只有当引用计数为0了，才回收物理空间\n否则只是将引用计数-1",
      "line": 60
    }
  ],
  "ref": "cow"
}